const PRIVACY = "This Privacy Policy explains how the Nano Banana mobile application (the “App”) handles information when you create or edit AI-generated images, generate videos, use AI Chat, manage subscriptions, and contact support. The App is independently operated by Sophia Baumgartner (\"we\", \"us\", \"our\").\n\n**IN BRIEF** Creative history is stored on your device. Content you submit for AI processing is transmitted directly to the relevant AI provider. Apple and Apphud support in-app subscriptions. The App does not display advertising or operate a public gallery.\n\n## Who is responsible for the App\n\nSophia Baumgartner, Woltmannweg 18B, 12209 Berlin, Germany, is responsible for the operation of the App and for determining the purposes of personal-data processing described here, where applicable. Privacy questions may be sent to sophia@baumgartnerapp.click.\n\n**Signed trademark authorization.** The Nano Banana name is used under a signed Trademark and Brand Use Authorization Agreement between Google LLC and Sophia Baumgartner, effective 14 October 2026. The agreement expressly authorizes Sophia Baumgartner to use “Nano Banana” directly in the App’s name/title in Apple’s App Store, as well as in related App Store materials. Google LLC retains ownership of its trademarks. The App is independently developed and operated by Sophia Baumgartner; the authorization does not make Google LLC the operator of the App or responsible for the personal-data processing described in this Policy.\n\n## Information handled by the App\n\n### 2.1 Creative content and generation requests\n\nDepending on the feature you choose, the App handles text prompts, editing instructions, reference photographs or other images you select or capture, generated images and videos, generation preferences (such as style, aspect ratio, duration or resolution), and locally saved history or favorites. Content submitted to an AI feature is sent to the relevant provider to generate or modify the requested result.\n\n### 2.2 AI Chat messages and attachments\n\nAI Chat lets you send text messages and attach an image selected from your photo library or captured with the camera. To respond to a message, the App sends the relevant text, conversational context and any attached image directly to OpenAI. Images are transmitted as part of the API request, including in an encoded image form. The App keeps chat sessions locally, including attached images, for up to 50 recent conversations. It does not operate a separate server-based chat archive.\n\n### 2.3 Photos, camera and exported files\n\nThe App requests camera and photo-library access only to enable functions you use, such as selecting a photo, capturing an image or saving generated media to your device. Access is governed by your device settings. A photo is not submitted to an AI provider merely because the App has permission to access photos; submission occurs when you use a feature that sends that selected content for processing. Saved or shared copies outside the App are managed by the destination you choose.\n\n### 2.4 Subscriptions and related identifiers\n\nPaid features are offered through Apple in-app subscriptions. Apple handles the billing process. ApphudSDK is used to manage purchase records, subscription status and access entitlements. For these purposes, Apphud may process transaction information, product identifiers, an Apphud-generated app user identifier and limited technical or device-related information. We do not receive your full payment-card details from Apple.\n\n### 2.5 Support communications and technical connection data\n\nIf you email support, we process the address and information you provide in order to answer your request. When the App connects directly to AI services or Apphud, those services may also receive routine network and request metadata, such as IP address, request timing or technical information necessary to deliver and secure the service, subject to their own terms and data practices.\n\n## Why information is processed\n\nWe process information only for purposes connected with providing and administering the App:\n\n- To perform the requested AI task, produce responses and media, and provide local history and favorites (performance of the service you request).\n- To activate, validate and administer subscriptions and to help prevent purchase-related errors or fraud (performance of our contract and legitimate interests).\n- To respond to support messages and maintain service reliability and security (legitimate interests, and where applicable performance of a contract).\n- To meet obligations under applicable law, including lawful requests and relevant transaction record requirements (legal obligation).\n\nWhere consent is required by applicable law, we rely on consent for the relevant processing. Device-level camera or photo permissions can be changed in system settings. You may choose not to submit particular text or images for AI processing, but the corresponding feature cannot work without the necessary input.\n\n## External providers and disclosures\n\n**fal.ai —** The App transmits prompts and user-selected images or other relevant generation inputs directly to fal.ai for image creation, photo editing and AI video generation. The provider processes requests and returns the resulting content.\n\n**OpenAI —** AI Chat text, conversation context and any attached images are sent directly to OpenAI to generate AI responses. OpenAI may process request data and service metadata under its applicable API arrangements and policies.\n\n**Apple and Apphud —** Apple manages App Store subscriptions and payments. Apphud is used for subscription verification, entitlement management and associated purchase information.\n\nThese parties process relevant information for their respective functions. We do not provide an in-app public gallery, social feed or user-to-user messaging service, and we do not sell user content to advertisers or use it for cross-app advertising tracking. The App does not include a separate general-purpose analytics SDK, Firebase, push notifications or a dedicated crash-reporting service. Apphud may provide subscription-related reporting as part of its subscription-management functions.\n\n## Local storage and retention\n\nGeneration history, prompts, generated images and videos, favorites, and AI Chat sessions are stored locally in the App’s storage on your device. The AI Chat history is limited to the 50 most recent conversations, and chat image attachments are kept with the corresponding local sessions. You can manage content through the App’s available history and deletion controls.\n\nDeleting the App removes its locally stored data from the device, subject to device or system-backup behavior. Images or videos that you separately saved to your Photos library or exported elsewhere are not removed by uninstalling the App. Subscription records held by Apple or Apphud, and data processed by AI providers, are governed by their applicable retention arrangements and legal obligations.\n\nWe do not maintain our own backend database of generated content or AI Chat history. However, the absence of our own server storage does not mean that third-party AI providers never retain requests or technical records. Their storage and deletion practices may differ and are described by their own applicable terms, policies and customer agreements; we do not represent a fixed retention period for those providers.\n\n## International processing\n\nThe AI and subscription services used by the App may process data in countries outside Germany or the European Economic Area, including the United States. Where applicable, such transfers must be handled under the relevant legal mechanisms and safeguards. You can review the providers’ published information for further details of their processing locations and protections.\n\n## Security and your choices\n\nWe rely on the device’s application storage and operating-system permissions for local content, and on the technical safeguards used by the external providers for transmitted requests. No transmission or storage system can be guaranteed completely secure. Avoid including passwords, confidential documents or third-party personal information in AI requests unless you have a lawful reason to do so and accept the necessary external processing.\n\nYou can deny or later revoke camera or photo-library permission in your device settings; some functions may no longer work. You can remove content using available in-app controls, delete the App to remove local data, cancel subscriptions in your Apple account and contact us with privacy questions or requests.\n\n## Your data-protection rights\n\nIf the General Data Protection Regulation or another applicable privacy law applies to you, you may have rights to request access to, correction or deletion of personal data, restriction of processing, data portability, and to object to certain processing. If we rely on consent, you may withdraw it without affecting prior lawful processing. These rights depend on the circumstances and legal exceptions.\n\nFor requests concerning information under our control, contact sophia@baumgartnerapp.click. Because creative history is held locally rather than in a developer-managed account, we may not be able to retrieve it remotely. Some data is held by Apple, Apphud or AI providers and may also be subject to their own request channels. You may lodge a complaint with a competent data-protection supervisory authority, including one in your country of residence in the EU.\n\n## Children and third-party content\n\nThe App is a general creative tool, not a service designed specifically for children. Where a user is not legally able to authorize the relevant use or processing independently, any required parent or guardian authorization must be obtained. Please do not upload images of other people or personal information without an appropriate legal basis or permission.\n\n## Changes to this Policy\n\nWe may update this Policy if the App, its service providers or applicable requirements change. The revised version will show its effective date and will be made available through the App or its listing. Material changes will be communicated when required by law.\n\n## Provider information\n\nFurther information about the external services is available in their published materials:\n\n- fal.ai — [Privacy Policy](https://fal.ai/legal/privacy-policy)\n- OpenAI — [API data controls](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/your-data)\n- Apphud — [Privacy Policy](https://apphud.com/legal/privacy)\n- Apple — [Privacy](https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/)\n\n## Contact\n\n**Operator / data controller:** Sophia Baumgartner\nWoltmannweg 18B, 12209 Berlin, Germany\n**Support and privacy requests:** sophia@baumgartnerapp.click";

const TERMS = "These Terms of Use (the “Terms”) govern your use of the Nano Banana mobile application (the “App”), operated by Sophia Baumgartner, Woltmannweg 18B, 12209 Berlin, Germany (“we”, “us”, “our”). By downloading, accessing or using the App, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the App.\n\n**PLEASE NOTE** The App provides AI-powered creative tools, including image generation, photo editing, video creation and AI Chat. Some functionality requires a paid Apple subscription and processing by external AI providers.\n\n## The App and its operator\n\nThe App allows users to generate images from text, edit existing images by written instructions, produce AI video from text or images, choose visual styles and generation settings, communicate with an AI assistant (including by attaching images), and organize creations using local history and favorites. You may save or export eligible results to your device.\n\n**Signed brand authorization.** Google LLC and Sophia Baumgartner have signed a Trademark and Brand Use Authorization Agreement effective 14 October 2026. Google expressly authorized Sophia Baumgartner to use “Nano Banana” in the App’s primary name (the App Name field) on Apple’s App Store and in associated listing materials. The App is independently developed and operated by Sophia Baumgartner, not by Google LLC, which is not a party to these Terms.\n\n## Eligibility and responsible use\n\nYou may use the App only if you can legally enter into these Terms, or if any permission required from your parent or guardian has been obtained. You must comply with applicable laws, Apple’s platform rules and these Terms. You are responsible for the content you choose to submit and for your use of generated results.\n\n## Your content and permissions\n\n“Your Content” includes prompts, chat messages, photographs, reference images and other material you submit, as well as creative files that you choose to save or export. You retain any rights you have in the material you supply. You confirm that you have the rights, permissions and legal basis necessary to provide Your Content and to request the relevant processing, including where it depicts or identifies another person.\n\nYou grant us a limited, non-exclusive permission to process, transmit and technically handle Your Content as needed to deliver the functions you request, including transmission to the AI providers described in our Privacy Policy. This permission is for providing and operating the App; it does not transfer ownership of Your Content to us.\n\nYou control whether to permit the App to access your camera and photo library through device settings. Some features require those permissions or your selection of media. The App may save generated media to your Photos library at your request. Exported copies may remain outside the App and are your responsibility to manage.\n\n## AI-generated results and limitations\n\nGenerative AI may produce inaccurate, unexpected, incomplete, offensive or similar-to-existing results. Outputs are not guaranteed to be unique, factual, suitable for a particular purpose, free of third-party rights, or legally protectable. You are responsible for reviewing results before publishing, distributing or otherwise relying on them, particularly when they depict real persons or are used in professional, commercial or consequential settings.\n\nAs between you and us, and subject to applicable law and third-party rights, we do not claim ownership of content solely because it was generated for you through the App. This statement is not a guarantee that copyright or other exclusive rights arise in any particular output; applicable law and provider conditions may affect your rights and permitted uses.\n\nAI Chat responses are provided for general creative assistance and informational purposes and are not professional legal, medical, financial or other regulated advice. You should independently verify information before relying on it.\n\n## AI providers and external services\n\nThe App uses fal.ai for image and video-related generation or editing and OpenAI for AI Chat responses. Relevant prompts, images, selected attachments and conversational context are transmitted directly from the App to the provider needed for the requested feature. External providers may have their own service policies, safety restrictions, availability conditions and data-processing arrangements.\n\nAI processing depends on network connectivity and the operation of those providers. Features, models, processing times, available formats, quality and capacity may change or become unavailable. We do not guarantee uninterrupted access, a particular output or a fixed generation time. See the Privacy Policy for details about transmitted data and local storage.\n\n## Prohibited conduct\n\nYou must not use the App to:\n\n- Break the law, violate the rights or privacy of others, or upload material you are not authorized to use.\n- Create or distribute exploitative, abusive, harassing, fraudulent or unlawfully deceptive content, including prohibited sexual material involving minors or non-consensual intimate content.\n- Impersonate another person deceptively, infringe intellectual-property rights or misrepresent AI-generated material in a way that is unlawful.\n- Attempt to bypass content safeguards, access restrictions or subscription checks, interfere with the App or service infrastructure, or reverse-engineer components except where applicable law expressly permits it.\n\nWe may restrict access to particular functions or decline processing where necessary to enforce these Terms, respond to legal requirements, or follow applicable provider safety rules, subject to your mandatory rights.\n\n## Subscriptions, renewal and billing\n\nSome or all premium features may require an auto-renewable subscription purchased using Apple In-App Purchase. Available plans, trial or promotional offers (if any), the billing period, the price and applicable conditions are shown in the App Store purchase interface before you confirm a purchase. The subscription renews automatically at the end of each period unless you cancel it using your Apple account before renewal under Apple’s applicable rules.\n\nApple processes payments and manages billing, renewals, cancellation and applicable refund requests. Apphud assists with subscription validation and access entitlements. You can view or cancel subscriptions through Settings on your device or Apple’s subscription management page. Deleting the App does not cancel an active subscription. Cancellation generally stops future renewals; access already paid for continues according to Apple’s terms and the applicable offer.\n\nPayment disputes and refund requests are handled through Apple’s applicable procedures, subject to mandatory consumer-protection laws. Any rights you have under applicable law are not limited by this section. If a subscription cannot be verified, premium functions may be unavailable until entitlement is restored.\n\n## Local storage and deletion\n\nThe App stores generation history, favorites and AI Chat sessions locally on your device. Up to 50 recent AI Chat conversations, including saved image attachments, may be kept in local application storage. The App does not operate its own remote archive of your chats or generated files. Deleting the App removes its local application data from your device, although device backups and separately exported or Photos-library files may remain. AI providers and subscription partners may retain information under their applicable policies, as explained in the Privacy Policy.\n\n## Intellectual property and App license\n\nThe App’s source code, interface, design, proprietary software and original service materials are protected by applicable intellectual-property law. Subject to your compliance with these Terms and Apple’s applicable rules, we grant you a personal, limited, revocable, non-exclusive, non-transferable license to use the App on devices you own or control for lawful purposes. No ownership in the App or its software is transferred to you.\n\n**Trademark ownership.** Nano Banana and related marks remain the property of Google LLC or their respective rights holders. The signed authorization applies to Sophia Baumgartner’s use for this App, including its App Store name, and does not transfer ownership or grant users separate rights in Google trademarks.\n\n## Privacy\n\nOur Privacy Policy explains the handling of prompts, selected images, AI Chat content, locally stored data, subscription information and support messages. By using AI features, you acknowledge that the input needed to fulfill your request is transmitted to the relevant external AI service. Please review the Privacy Policy before submitting personal or confidential content.\n\n## Availability, updates and termination\n\nWe may maintain, update, modify or discontinue features to improve performance, address safety issues, satisfy legal requirements or adapt to changes in external services. Where legally required, we will provide notice and preserve applicable consumer rights. You may stop using the App at any time; you remain responsible for managing any active subscription through Apple.\n\nWe may suspend or limit access for a serious violation of these Terms or legal requirements, provided such action is proportionate and consistent with applicable law. Sections that by their nature should survive termination, including liability provisions and intellectual-property protections, will continue to apply as permitted by law.\n\n## Warranties and liability\n\nWe aim to provide a functional creative application, but AI-generated outputs and third-party services may be variable. To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the App is provided without guarantees of uninterrupted availability or suitability for a specific outcome. We are not responsible for consequences of relying on unverified AI outputs or for user-supplied content that violates rights or laws.\n\nNothing in these Terms excludes or restricts liability that cannot lawfully be excluded, including liability for intent, gross negligence, injury to life, body or health where applicable, or mandatory consumer rights. Any other limitations apply only to the extent permitted by the law governing your relationship with us.\n\n## Governing law and consumer protection\n\nThese Terms are governed by the laws of Germany, without depriving consumers of mandatory protections available under the law of their habitual residence when those protections apply. Any dispute shall be handled by a court with jurisdiction under applicable law. You retain mandatory statutory rights regardless of these Terms.\n\n## Changes to these Terms\n\nWe may revise these Terms to reflect legal requirements, product developments or changes in service providers. The latest version will state its effective date and be available through the App or its listing. Where applicable law requires advance notice or additional consent for material changes, we will comply with those requirements.\n\n## Contact\n\nFor questions about the App, these Terms, subscriptions or support, contact:\n\nSophia Baumgartner\nWoltmannweg 18B, 12209 Berlin, Germany\n**Email:** sophia@baumgartnerapp.click";

